<title>SWEDEN: BOFORS WINS U.S. ARMY AMMUNITION ORDER.</title>
<headline>BOFORS WINS U.S. ARMY AMMUNITION ORDER.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bofors Carl Gustaf AB, a unit of Swedish defence industry group Celsius, said on Thursday it had received an order for small arms armour-piercing ammunition from the U.S. army.</p>
<p>The order is initially worth 60 million crowns with deliveries to start from this year with an option for a further 60 million crowns of ammunition.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said Bofors had previously received a small order from the U.S. army but this contract for the Carl Gustaf armour- piercing ammunition was the largest to date.</p>
<p>The ammunition will be produced at Bofors' works at Karlsborg in Sweden.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
